Theorem 2.5 (Extreme value Theorem)

If X ⊆ R'' is compact and f: X -> R is continuous, then f must have both a global maximum and a global minimum somewhere on X. 
That is, there must exist points a(sub(max)) and a(sub(min)) in X such that, for all x ∈ X, 

		f(a(sub(min))) =< f(x) =< f(a(sub(min)))
