The Lagrange Multiplier

Theorem 3.1

Let X be open in R'' and f, g: X -> R be functions of class C¹. 
Let S = {x ∈ X | g(x) = c } denote the leve set of g at height c. 
Then if f |s (the restriction of f to S) has an extremum at a point x₀ ∈ S such that ∇g(x₀) != 0, there must be some scalar λ such that 

		∇f(x₀) = λ∇g(x₀)

